 Further information on configuring Microsoft.Logging can be found [at Microsoft docs](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/extensions/logging?tabs=command-line)
 
+### Custom thread pools
+
+If you derive from `TaskSchedulingThreadPool`, the signature of `GetDefaultScheduler` has changed to accept a
+`CancellationToken`. The token is signaled once the thread pool has been shut down and no more tasks are running,
+so that any resources (such as dedicated threads) held by the task scheduler can be released.
+
+```csharp
+// 3.x
+protected override TaskScheduler GetDefaultScheduler() { ... }
+
+// 4.x
+protected override TaskScheduler GetDefaultScheduler(CancellationToken cancellationToken) { ... }
+```
+
 ### JSON Serialization
 
 To configure JSON serialization to be used in job store instead of old `UseJsonSerializer` you should now use either `UseSystemTextJsonSerializer` or `UseNewtonsoftJsonSerializer`
